    {
      "sectionId": "section-disclaimer",
      "heading": "Understanding RPGBOT’s Rating System",
      "sourceAnchor": "disclaimer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "RPGBOT uses a color coding scheme which is simple to understand and easy to read at a glance. This system is designed to help players make informed decisions for their dnd character builds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Red"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Bad, useless options, or options which\n\t\tare extremely situational. Nearly never useful."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Orange"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": OK options, or useful options\n\t\tthat only apply in rare circumstances. Useful sometimes."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Green"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Good options. Useful often."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Blue"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Fantastic options, often essential\n\t\tto the function of your character. Useful very frequently."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The advice offered below is based on the current "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "State of the 2014 DnD 5e Character Optimization Meta",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/state-of-the-meta/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " as of when the article was last updated. Keep in mind that the state of the meta periodically changes as new source materials are released, and the article will be updated accordingly as time allows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We will not include 3rd-party content, Unearthed Arcnaa content, or homebrew in guides for official content because we can’t assume that your game will allow them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Classes",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes",
      "blocks": []
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-artificer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Artificer",
      "sourceAnchor": "artificer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-artificer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Artificers get proficiency in firearms automatically and have very little\n\treason to use Strength checks, so the Giff’s entire contribution to the\n\tArtificer is the ability to ignore Loading with firearms, which can be\n\treplaced with an infusion."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-barbarian",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Barbarian",
      "sourceAnchor": "barbarian",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-barbarian-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Advantage on Strength checks can be replaced by Rage, and barbarians are\n\tlocked into melee too heavily for firearms to be helpful."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-bard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Bard",
      "sourceAnchor": "bard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-bard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Martial bards (swords and valor) may find firearms a helpful addition to the\n\tBard’s weapon options, and Advantage on Strength checks can make Strength\n\t(Athletics) very effective when combined with Expertise even if your Strength\n\tis poor."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-cleric",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Cleric",
      "sourceAnchor": "cleric",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-cleric-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Weapons are a poor choice for clerics and without Extra attack there is\n\trarely a good reason to use Strength (Athletics), so advantage on Strength\n\tchecks is rarely useful."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-druid",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Druid",
      "sourceAnchor": "druid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-druid-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Weapons are a poor choice for most druid, and the ones that use weapons don’t\n\tuse firearms. Without Extra attack there is rarely a good reason to use\n\tStrength (Athletics), so advantage on Strength checks is rarely useful."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-fighter",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Fighter",
      "sourceAnchor": "fighter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fighter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The obvious and easy choice for a race so martially-inclined."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fighter-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Melee builds should absolutely lean into Hippo Build’s Advantage on Strength checks to "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Grapple/Shove",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/grapple/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " your enemies. Advantage isn’t as good as Expertise mathematically, but it’s close enough for most of your career. Put enemies on the ground. You can also combine it with Expertise via Skill Expert for the most assurance possible short of reliable talent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fighter-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Ranged builds will enjoy the Giff’s Firearm’s Mastery, which gives you a big\n\tchunk of the\n\t"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Gunner",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/feats/gunner/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " feat,\n\twhich means that you can play a gun user right from level 1 without playing\n\tyet another variant human. Grab Fighting Style (Archery) and Sharpshooter and\n\tyou’re ready to deal some damage."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fighter-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Ranged builds should strongly consider proficiency in Athletics and a splash\n\tof Strength to support it. With Advantage on Strength checks and Extra Attack\n\tthat gives you more attacks than anyone else, it’s easy to Shove an enemy out\n\tof reach then get right back to shooting."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-monk",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Monk",
      "sourceAnchor": "monk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-monk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An easy source of Advantage is a massive boon for monks, but with typically poor Strength most monks can’t effectively Shove enemies prone. With a splash of Strength, proficiency in Athletics, and Hippo Build, Shove suddenly becomes a viable option for the monk. Knock your enemy prone then hit them with Flurry of Blows."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-paladin",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Paladin",
      "sourceAnchor": "paladin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-paladin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Paladins struggle to fight at range, so Firearms Mastery is largely wasted,\n\tbut Hippo Build’s advantage on Strength checks is a great way to make\n\tGrapple/Shove as useful for the Paladin as it is for the Barbarian and the\n\tFighter. Put your enemies on the ground and fish for critical smites."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ranger",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Ranger",
      "sourceAnchor": "ranger",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ranger-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Much like the Fighter, rangers built for ranged combat will benefit from\n\tFirearm Mastery, getting a bit more damage from muskets than you would from\n\tcrossbows and longbows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ranger-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Rangers built around Strength may find Hippo Build useful if you want to get\n\tinto grappling/shoving, but two-handed melee weapons are a difficult choice\n\tfor rangers and you need a free hand to do either."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-rogue",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Rogue",
      "sourceAnchor": "rogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-rogue-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Despite their absolute lack of subtlety, you can sneak attack with muskets.\n\tAt low levels, the Musket’s d12 damage die is much better than the d6 you’ll\n\tget from the Rogue’s other ranged weapon options. Unfortunately, that’s really\n\tthe only thing that the Giff adds to the Rogue."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-rogue-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Combining the Rogue’s easy access to Expertise with Hippo Build to get really\n\tgood at Athletics is very tempting, but save this for characters taking a\n\tclass dip into rogue. Without Extra Attack, you don’t want to dedicate an\n\tentire turn to a single grapple or shove."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-sorcerer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Sorcerer",
      "sourceAnchor": "sorcerer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-sorcerer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "You don’t need guns and you certainly shouldn’t be making Strength checks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-sorcerer-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If you want a gun-wielding sorcerer and you’re open to 3rd-party content,\n\tcheck out our\n\t"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Black Powder Sorcery Handbook",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/classes/kobold-presss-black-powder-sorcery/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". Then you can be a space hippo magically weilding a brace of pistols fueled\n\tby your ancestral attachment to black powder firearms. Somehow that’s the most\n\tgiff thing I can think of, and giff canonically can’t use magic (player\n\tcharacters get to be special, of course)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-warlock",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Warlock",
      "sourceAnchor": "warlock",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-warlock-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Tragically, Pact of the Blade doesn’t function with firearms, so there’s\n\tnothing here for the Giff."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-wizard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Wizard",
      "sourceAnchor": "wizard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-wizard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "You don’t need guns and you certainly shouldn’t be making Strength checks."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
